        <h2 id="planned" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Planned</h2>
        <span class="status-chip" data-status="Partly built">Partly built</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prose mt-4 text-base">
      <p>
        These pages exist in the app, but only part of the feature is behind them.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-none space-y-0 divide-y divide-line pl-0">
        <li class="py-3"><strong>OF Manager:</strong> every section, from Home to OF settings, is there; most show placeholder data and few controls save. New post and Add to story do post, and Statistics reads real figures.</li>
        <li class="py-3"><strong>Fansly Manager:</strong> Notifications, Lists, Scheduled Posts and Earning Statistics are built, behind a setting; the other 12 pages show a NotBuiltYet empty state.</li>
        <li class="py-3"><strong>Auto-renew campaigns:</strong> not built; the fan list only flags fans with auto-renew off.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To pick one up, check the <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/docs/routes.md">route list</a> and open a pull request.
        To ask for something new, <a href="{{ site.repo }}/issues/new">open an issue</a>.
      </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="known-gaps" class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 ring-1 ring-black/10">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
        <h2 id="known-gaps" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Known gaps</h2>
        <span class="status-chip" data-status="Not built">Not built</span>
      </div>
      <div class="prose mt-4 text-base">
      <p>
        Security work the code still needs; the <a href="{{ '/help/#security' | url }}">security notes</a> describe the
        same five. Until they are fixed, run it only on a private network or over a VPN (WireGuard or Tailscale).
      </p>
      <ul class="list-none space-y-0 divide-y divide-line pl-0">
        <li class="py-3"><strong>Closing sign-up (Not built, known gap):</strong> sign-up has no setting and needs no share token; anyone who can reach the server can register at <code>/login</code>.</li>
        <li class="py-3"><strong>Hiding the roster (Not built, known gap):</strong> any registered account can list every user and every creator account on the server.</li>
        <li class="py-3"><strong>Hashed passwords (Not built, known gap):</strong> the owner's and chatters' dashboard passwords are stored in plain text in <code>service/chatterly.db</code>. Creators' OnlyFans passwords never reach the server.</li>
        <li class="py-3"><strong>A login for the lanes panel (Not built, known gap):</strong> the lanes panel (the relay's rate-limit page at <code>/lanes-panel</code>) can change the limits and restart the relay with no login or share token.</li>
        <li class="py-3"><strong>A role check on admin actions (Not built, known gap):</strong> <code>ADMIN_PASSWORD</code> alone unlocks "view as another user", transfer and delete for any signed-in account that knows it.</li>
      </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <div class="prose mt-12">
    <h2>Not on the roadmap</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>AI:</strong> No AI chatter that sells on its own. The old AI Chatter, AI Upseller and tip rewards were
      removed. What writes to fans today is Auto-reply (one casual line, never a pitch) and Get to know fans; the AI
      Copilot only suggests, and a person presses Send.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Support:</strong> no help desk, no SLA and no uptime figure. The README, the code, GitHub issues and the
      in-app help bot.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
